<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>The fountain plaza (angles in the same segment and opposite angles)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A circular plaza has a fountain in the middle, and \(O\) is the centre of the plaza.
Two lamp posts, \(A\) and \(B\), stand on its edge. A photographer at \(P\) on the edge sees both lamp posts, and angle \(APB = {@v@}^\circ\).
A second photographer stands at \(Q\) on the same side of \(AB\) as \(P\), and a street artist stands at \(R\) on the opposite side of \(AB\). All of \(P\), \(Q\) and \(R\) are on the edge of the plaza.</p>

<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="A circular plaza with centre O and a fountain in the middle. Lamp posts A and B are on the edge. Photographers P and Q are on the major arc, and the artist R is on the minor arc between A and B. The angle at P is {#v#} degrees.">
[[jsxgraph width="380px" height="400px"]]
var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[-1.6,1.6,1.6,-1.6], axis:false, showCopyright:false, showNavigation:false, keepAspectRatio:true});
var r = Math.PI/180;
var v = {#v#}, pa = {#pa#}, qa = {#qa#};
function pt(nm, deg, col) {
  var t = deg*r;
  return board.create('point',[Math.cos(t),Math.sin(t)],{name:nm,fixed:true,size:5,strokeColor:col,fillColor:col,
    label:{offset:[16*Math.cos(t)-4,16*Math.sin(t)-4],strokeColor:col}});
}
board.create('circle',[[0,0],1],{fixed:true,strokeColor:'#0f766e',strokeWidth:4,fillColor:'#99f6e4',fillOpacity:0.45,highlight:false});
board.create('circle',[[0,0],0.12],{fixed:true,strokeColor:'#0369a1',fillColor:'#38bdf8',fillOpacity:0.9,highlight:false});
var O = board.create('point',[0,0],{name:'O',fixed:true,size:3,strokeColor:'#1e293b',fillColor:'#1e293b',label:{offset:[8,-18]}});
var A = pt('A', 90+v, '#ea580c');
var B = pt('B', 90-v, '#ea580c');
var P = pt('P', pa, '#2563eb');
var Q = pt('Q', qa, '#16a34a');
var R = pt('R', 90, '#db2777');
board.create('segment',[A,B],{fixed:true,strokeColor:'#7c3aed',strokeWidth:2,dash:2});
board.create('segment',[P,A],{fixed:true,strokeColor:'#2563eb',strokeWidth:2});
board.create('segment',[P,B],{fixed:true,strokeColor:'#2563eb',strokeWidth:2});
board.create('segment',[Q,A],{fixed:true,strokeColor:'#16a34a',strokeWidth:2});
board.create('segment',[Q,B],{fixed:true,strokeColor:'#16a34a',strokeWidth:2});
board.create('segment',[R,A],{fixed:true,strokeColor:'#db2777',strokeWidth:2});
board.create('segment',[R,B],{fixed:true,strokeColor:'#db2777',strokeWidth:2});
board.create('segment',[O,A],{fixed:true,strokeColor:'#94a3b8',strokeWidth:2,dash:3});
board.create('segment',[O,B],{fixed:true,strokeColor:'#94a3b8',strokeWidth:2,dash:3});
board.create('angle',[B,P,A],{radius:0.3,fillColor:'#93c5fd',fillOpacity:0.9,strokeColor:'#2563eb',withLabel:false});
board.create('angle',[B,Q,A],{radius:0.3,fillColor:'#86efac',fillOpacity:0.9,strokeColor:'#16a34a',withLabel:false});
board.create('angle',[A,R,B],{radius:0.2,fillColor:'#f9a8d4',fillOpacity:0.9,strokeColor:'#db2777',withLabel:false});
function angLabel(brd, A, V, C, t) { var ax = A.X() - V.X(), ay = A.Y() - V.Y(), cx = C.X() - V.X(), cy = C.Y() - V.Y(); var la = Math.sqrt(ax*ax + ay*ay), lc = Math.sqrt(cx*cx + cy*cy); var ux = ax/la + cx/lc, uy = ay/la + cy/lc, lu = Math.sqrt(ux*ux + uy*uy); var h = Math.acos(Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, (ax*cx + ay*cy)/(la*lc))))/2; var d = Math.min(0.72, Math.max(0.44, 0.15/Math.tan(h))); brd.create('text', [V.X() + d*ux/lu, V.Y() + d*uy/lu, t], {anchorX:'middle', anchorY:'middle', fontSize:13, fixed:true, highlight:false, cssStyle:'background:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);padding:0 2px;border-radius:3px'}); }
angLabel(board, B, P, A, '{#v#}°');
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>

<p>(a) Find angle \(AQB\). [[input:ans1]]\(^\circ\) [[validation:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p>(b) Find angle \(ARB\). [[input:ans2]]\(^\circ\) [[validation:ans2]]</p>
<div>[[feedback:prt2]]</div>

<p>(c) Find angle \(AOB\). [[input:ans3]]\(^\circ\) [[validation:ans3]]</p>
<div>[[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h4>Worked solution</h4>
<p><strong>(a)</strong> \(P\) and \(Q\) are on the same side of \(AB\), so angles in the same segment are equal:
\(AQB = {@v@}^\circ\).</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> \(R\) is on the opposite side of \(AB\) from \(P\), so \(R\) and \(P\) are opposite corners of a cyclic quadrilateral:
\(ARB = 180 - {@v@} = {@ta2@}^\circ\).</p>
<p><strong>(c)</strong> The angle at the centre is twice the angle at the circumference:
\(AOB = 2 \times {@v@} = {@ta3@}^\circ\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
